-A technique where the full 3D orientation of the volume corresponding to each tilt image is directly optimized during the INR training process to correct for tilt axis errors and misalignment. Sets itself apart by jointly optimizing network weights and pose parameters rather than assuming fixed poses. Choose when dealing with electron tomography data subject to rotational misalignment. Large misalignment increases convergence epochs, so coarse preprocessing is recommended.
+### Inline Alignment / Pose Optimization
+A technique where the full 3D orientation of the volume corresponding to each tilt image is directly optimized during the INR training process to correct for tilt axis errors and misalignment. Sets itself apart by jointly optimizing network weights and pose parameters rather than assuming fixed poses. Choose when dealing with electron tomography data subject to rotational misalignment. Large misalignment increases convergence epochs, so coarse preprocessing is recommended [S3, unofficial].
 
